The meson build generates libfuse_config.h; this interface-only use supplies the three version
macros as cc_library defines instead (see libfuse.BUILD.bazel), so the include becomes conditional
rather than a hard requirement clang-tidy's parse cannot satisfy for a generated header. The hunk
context is deliberately minimal: a unified diff renders an empty context line as a lone space,
which the trim-trailing-whitespace hook would strip, corrupting the patch.
--- a/include/fuse_common.h
+++ b/include/fuse_common.h
@@ -21,1 +21,3 @@
+#if __has_include("libfuse_config.h")
 #include "libfuse_config.h"
+#endif
